{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774883453,"nonce":"5EFeQlVl18L3pb8vAe4iZIRTQZE=","title":"nightshift upstream — propose template changes back to canonical repo","message":"Add a `nightshift upstream` command that lets downstream projects propose prompt improvements back to the canonical templates in the agent-worker repo.\n\n## Current State\n\n- `nightshift upgrade` pulls canonical → project (one-way)\n- No reverse flow exists\n- Project-specific prompt improvements stay siloed\n\n## Proposed: `nightshift upstream`\n\n### Flow\n\n1. Diffs local WORKFLOW.md and REVIEW.md prompt sections against canonical templates (reuses `core/upgrade.py` diffing machinery, reversed)\n2. Runs client-side validation filters (see guardrails below)\n3. Shows diff to user for confirmation\n4. Files a git-bug issue in the upstream repo with the proposed diff\n\nThe upstream repo is found via `TEMPLATES_DIR` (already resolved relative to the installed package).\n\n### Operation Types\n\nEach upstream proposal must declare its type:\n\n- **Add** — new rule/section. Must not overlap semantically with existing rules.\n- **Replace** — improved version of an existing rule. Proposal explicitly marks which lines are replaced. Replacement must be same length or shorter.\n- **Consolidate** — merge multiple rules into fewer. Used when template approaches the soft limit. Must preserve all original intents.\n\n### Guardrails\n\n**Client-side filters (in `nightshift upstream`, before filing):**\n- Scan diff for project-specific markers (repo names, framework names, absolute paths, specific file references). Reject or warn.\n- Reject if an Add operation increases prompt size beyond the hard cap (150 lines).\n- Validate all Jinja2 variables are from the known set (`issue.title`, `issue.body`, `diff`, `related_context`, etc.).\n\n**Template lint suite (runs as pytest, gates agent work):**\n- No project-specific references (configurable blocklist)\n- No absolute paths or specific module references\n- Prompt size under hard cap (150 lines), warn at soft cap (100 lines)\n- All Jinja2 variables in known set\n- No semantic duplicates (fuzzy — checked by reviewing agent, not lint)\n\n**Agent review criteria (auto-reviewer checks these):**\n- Language is generic and project-agnostic\n- Replace operations preserve original intent\n- Consolidate operations don't drop any rule's intent\n- No contradictions with existing rules\n\n**Consolidation trigger:**\n- `nightshift upgrade` warns when template exceeds soft cap (100 lines): \"Template at N/150 lines — consider consolidation\"\n- Consolidation proposals reduce line count while preserving all intents\n\n**Provenance:** Each upstream issue records source project name for traceability.\n\n**Template versioning:** Minor bump for additive changes, major bump for behavioral changes (replacements, consolidations). `nightshift upgrade` shows major bumps as warnings requiring `--apply --force`.\n\n## Implementation Touches\n\n- `core/upgrade.py` — add `diff_against_canonical_reverse()`, operation type detection\n- `host/cli.py` — add `cmd_upstream` subcommand\n- `tests/test_template_lint.py` — new lint suite for canonical templates\n- `templates/` — add blocklist config for project-specific terms\n- `core/upgrade.py` — extend versioning for minor/major distinction\n\n## Requirements\n\nNew REQ (REQ-027 or similar). Extends REQ-024 (template versioning/upgrade).","files":null}]}